I just ascended an orcish rogue. This is my second ascension. I made
fewer mistakes this time (I didn't loose my memory to mindflayers, I
didn't open Rodney's tower before wearing my cloak of magic resistance,
and I didn't ever die.) My most notable mistake was forgetting to bring
the candelabrum and the bell with me from their stash at Orcustown when
I went for the book of the dead; I realized my mistake as I left the
tower with the book. The other major differences were my decision to
genocide liches (unlike the last ascension, which was genoless), that I
remembered to bring four scrolls of gold detection to the planes, and
the more difficult fight in Moloch's sanctum. Rodney showed up, and
double troubled (the first time I've seen that); I entered the inner
sanctum, blasted them both with WoD, then did the same to the high
priest (I had five wands of death, so I wasn't worrying about
conserving them). I took the amulet, but the undead, who I had failed
to clear out, slowed me down, and I was forced to kill Rodney a few
more times as I left. I didn't see him on my way up, though, until I
got the the Plane of Earth. He died without too much trouble, and I dug
my way over to the portal. Easy. Air was also fairly easy; the air
elementals seemed to pursue me more aggressively than last time, but
they were still not very tough. I had wasted a ?oGD, so on Fire, I
tried to get through without one, but I had to saw a couple of Archons,
got nervous, and used my last one, along with a wish (I had plenty
left) for two more to use on the Plane of Water. Here wasn't too
difficult, though I worried about my rings. I got through fine.
Like in my last ascension, I was primarily a melee character. I used a
+6 Stormbringer for most of the late game, and mostly just used my +7
elven daggers against Rodney, the riders, and a few other tough
monsters. I also had the bad luck to have my altar turn up last on the
Astral planes; I visited Neutral and Lawful altars before facing famine
and reaching the Chaotic altar. The same thing happened in my last
ascension, but I don't like the idea of the helm of opposite alignment,
so I didn't use one.
I remember finding two bones files; the first was just below Medusa; a
rogue who had choked on a pancake. Yes, a pancake. He yielded a good
set of rings, which I uncursed and IDed. That was all of the important
rings except for free action, which I finally found in the dungeon. The
second file was much more interesting. It was the bones of my first
character to make it past the castle; he was a barbarian who died in
Orcustown fighting both Orcus and Demogorgon. Orcus 'ported to the
stairs as soon as I showed up, and I had time to kill him before
Demogorgon showed up. I couldn't leave, since he would follow me up the
stairs, and I kept getting sick; I finally looked into all the things I
could do to cure sickness, drank a potion of Full Healing, consulted
the Demogorgon FAQ, burned Elbereth, and fled. I left the game to
think, then came back, got a cockatrice corpse, and killed Demogorgon
with it. The bones file had a [0:0] wand of wishing in it, which was a
nice extra, but never necessary, since I only spent one wish after this
point. After that fight, the rest of the ascension seems easy.



